  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This guide is for the version of the Earth Genasi published in Monsters of\n\tthe Multiverse. For the classic version of the Genasi, see our\n\t"
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Genasi Handbook",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/races/genasi/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Descendants of Dao, the genies native to the elemental plane of earth, the Earth Genasi’s traits are (somewhat) earth themed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Prior to Monsters of the Multiverse, Earth Walk only worked on rocky terrain.\n\tWhile this made sense thematically, it was also extremely limiting. Freed from\n\tthis restriction, you’re free to walk through difficult terrain created by\n\tplants, sand, etc."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Innate spellcasting is easily the Earth Genasi’s most notable trait. Pass Without Trace solves the challenge of stealth for your whole party, and since you can re-cast it with spell slots, you can bring it to any spellcasting class. The Earth Genasi’s unique ability to cast Blade Ward as a Bonus Action a few times per day may be the only way that Blade Ward could be better than the Dodge action. It’s very similar in concept and effect to the Goliath’s Stones Endurance, but notably you need to use it ahead of time."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
